Found by a coordinator feature-gap review of the LSP + extension, 2026-08-30.
Enabler for the quick-fix family (B036/B037/B038). Not a regression.

## Gap
`src/server/code_actions.rs` is 369 lines offering exactly TWO actions:
`quick_fix_did_you_mean` (:41) and `refactor_wrap_in_try_catch` (:88).
Meanwhile `TypeDiagnosticKind` (src/typecheck/checker.rs:28+) has ~25 variants,
most of them mechanically fixable.

The capability declaration is the blocker for the good version:

    src/server/mod.rs:1038
    code_action_provider: Some(CodeActionProviderCapability::Simple(true)),

`Simple(true)` advertises NO `codeActionKinds` and NO `resolve_provider`.
Consequences, all client-visible:
- VS Code cannot populate "Source Action..." (needs a `source.*` kind).
- `editor.codeActionsOnSave` cannot run our fixes — there is no
  `source.fixAll.*` kind to name.
- No "Fix all of this kind in file" / "in workspace".
- Every action's edit must be computed eagerly on every `textDocument/
  codeAction` request, because there is no resolve step to defer it to.

For a codebase like tests/fixtures/tm-editor-plus-plus (1428 warnings) the
difference between per-squiggle right-clicking and fix-on-save is the
difference between usable and not.

## Work
- Advertise `CodeActionProviderCapability::Options(CodeActionOptions { .. })`
  with an explicit `code_action_kinds` list: at minimum `QUICKFIX`,
  `SOURCE_FIX_ALL`, `REFACTOR_REWRITE`, and a namespaced
  `source.fixAll.openplanet`.
- Set `resolve_provider: Some(true)` and implement `codeAction/resolve` so the
  edit is computed only for the action the user actually picked. Keep the
  action list cheap to produce (title + kind + diagnostic only).
- Build the dispatch seam the fix families plug into: a registry mapping a
  `TypeDiagnosticKind` discriminant to a fix producer
  `fn(&Diagnostic, &SourceFile, &SymbolTable) -> Vec<CodeAction>`, so
  B036/B037/B038 add fixes without touching the request handler. Keep the
  interface small — one function, one enum arm.
- Implement `source.fixAll.openplanet`: collect every auto-applicable fix in
  the document, drop the ones whose edits overlap, apply the rest in one
  `WorkspaceEdit`. Overlap handling is the whole difficulty here; make it a
  pure, separately tested function.
- Implement ONE exemplar fix end-to-end through the new seam so the
  infrastructure is proven: use `StringByValueParam` (see B036), the simplest
  span replacement of the set.
- Extension side: nothing required, but confirm `editor.codeActionsOnSave`
  with `source.fixAll.openplanet` works against the built VSIX before closing.

## Design decision (coordinator, 2026-08-30)
Fixes are OFFERED but never auto-applied without the user opting in. The
`source.fixAll` kind exists so the user can wire it into `codeActionsOnSave`
themselves; we do not enable it by default. A checker warning is a suggestion,
and silently rewriting a user's parameter list on save is worse than the
warning it removes.

Actions must be marked `isPreferred` only where the fix is unambiguous and
lossless. `StringByValueParam` qualifies; anything offering two alternatives
(see B038) does not.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Existing tests in `src/server/code_actions.rs` `mod tests` (:224+) build a
`SymbolTable` fixture and assert over returned actions — follow that shape.

Red:
- `capability_advertises_quickfix_and_fixall_kinds`: the `initialize` result
  lists `source.fixAll.openplanet` (fails today: `Simple(true)` lists none).
- `code_action_resolve_computes_edit_lazily`: the action returned by
  `textDocument/codeAction` has `edit: None`, and `codeAction/resolve`
  populates it.
- `fix_all_applies_every_nonoverlapping_fix`: a document with 3 fixable
  diagnostics yields one `WorkspaceEdit` containing 3 edits.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):
- zero fixable diagnostics -> `fixAll` returns no action, not an empty edit
- two fixes whose spans OVERLAP -> exactly one applied, deterministically
  chosen, and the other still offered individually
- two fixes on the SAME line but disjoint spans -> both applied
- edits applied in descending span order so earlier edits do not invalidate
  later offsets (assert the resulting text, not just the edit count)
- a diagnostic from a DIFFERENT source (not ours) in the same range is ignored
- `only` filter in `CodeActionParams` honoured: requesting `quickfix` must not
  return the refactor, and requesting `source.fixAll` must not return
  per-diagnostic quick fixes
- resolve called on an action with no edit available -> returns the action
  unchanged, does not error
- the existing "Did you mean" and "Wrap in try/catch" actions still work and
  still carry their original kinds (regression guard)

## Related
Fix families: B036 (mechanical replacements), B037 (conversions/structural),
B038 (rename/const). All three depend on this seam.